🚀 Week 2 – Day 5 Arrays & Multi-Dimensional Arrays in Java ☕

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

Arrays are used to store **multiple values of the same data type** in a single variable.

👉 They are fundamental for:

✔ Data storage
✔ Problem solving
✔ DSA preparation

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔢 1. What is an Array?

An array is a fixed-size collection of similar elements.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Syntax

```java id="a1"
dataType[] arrayName;
```

---

📌 Declaration and Initialization

```java id="a2"
int[] numbers = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
```

---

📌 Accessing Elements

```java id="a3"
System.out.println(numbers[0]); // 10
System.out.println(numbers[2]); // 30
```

---

🔍 Array Indexing

* First index = `0`
* Last index = `length - 1`

---

🔁 Traversing an Array

🔹 Using for Loop

```java id="a4"
for (int i = 0; i < numbers.length; i++) {
    System.out.println(numbers[i]);
}
```

---

🔹 Using Enhanced for Loop

```java id="a5"
for (int num : numbers) {
    System.out.println(num);
}
```

---

📏 Array Properties

```java id="a6"
System.out.println(numbers.length);
```

---

⚠️ Common Error

```java id="a7"
System.out.println(numbers[10]);
```

👉 Causes:

```text id="a8"
ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
```

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧮 2. Multi-Dimensional Arrays

A multi-dimensional array is an array of arrays.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 2D Array Syntax

```java id="m1"
dataType[][] arrayName;
```

---

📌 Initialization

```java id="m2"
int[][] matrix = {
    {1, 2, 3},
    {4, 5, 6},
    {7, 8, 9}
};
```

---

📌 Accessing Elements

```java id="m3"
System.out.println(matrix[1][2]); // 6
```

---

🔁 Traversing 2D Array

```java id="m4"
for (int i = 0; i < matrix.length; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < matrix[i].length; j++) {
        System.out.print(matrix[i][j] + " ");
    }
    System.out.println();
}
```

---

📌 Jagged Arrays

Rows can have different lengths.

```java id="m5"
int[][] jagged = {
    {1, 2},
    {3, 4, 5},
    {6}
};
```

---

🎯 Advantages of Arrays

✔ Store multiple values efficiently
✔ Easy to process with loops
✔ Foundation for many data structures

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Limitations of Arrays

❌ Fixed size
❌ Same data type only
❌ Insertions/deletions are costly

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Real-World Uses

* Student marks
* Temperature records
* Game boards
* Matrices

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ Arrays store same-type elements
✔ Index starts at 0
✔ Use `.length` to get size
✔ 2D arrays represent tables/matrices
✔ Jagged arrays allow variable row sizes

